.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store
logs/
.venv/
venv/

# data/ is allow-listed, not deny-listed.
#
# Only the five files below ship. Everything else that lands in data/ is local
# scratch, and several of those working files carry Lenz's own verdict labels
# (lenz_verdict / lenz_score / lenz_reason). This repo must never publish a
# verdict label: the claims are sourced from Lenz, so shipping Lenz's answer
# alongside them would hand any reader a gold key the models were deliberately
# denied, and would contradict both the README and the paper's ethics
# statement. A deny-list would leak the next scratch file someone forgets to
# add; an allow-list fails closed.
data/*
!data/claims.json
!data/results.json
!data/results.jsonl
!data/results.csv
!data/LICENSE
